      "targeted_symptom": "S016",
      "patient_response": "Oh, gosh... um. I really hate to admit this, but... yeah, I guess I do that. I try so hard to be a good listener, I promise. It's just... sometimes when a guy on the crew or someone in a meeting is asking me something, I'll kind of, well, cut them off a little bit? \n\nBut it's really only because my brain is just moving so fast and I think I already know exactly where their question is going. I just want to be helpful and give them the answer right away so we can keep the job moving, you know? But then... I end up answering way too fast, and I'll realize a second later that I completely missed the actual important part of what they hadn't even said yet. \n\nI always feel terrible when it happens because I know it probably comes across as rude, and I swear I don't mean to be disrespectful at all. I just get a little too eager to fix the problem. Does that make sense? I really hope I'm not making myself sound like a jerk to work with. Am I giving you the right kind of examples?",
